On Wed, 26 Oct 2005, Doug Freyburger wrote:

> It's common for folks to use wizard mode or explore mode
> to solve puzzles.  If you want to do that in your current
> game and you save before going into explore mode, then
> quit no matter how your experiment turns out and you
> restore your saved game, is that still savescumming in
> your opinion?

Irrespective of your experiment, you cannot avoid getting additional
information about your normal game ("The captain zaps a wand of death!
The death ray whizzes by you!"; "The orc hurls a cyan potion! The vial
crashes on your head and breaks into shards. Something seems to be holding
you.") before you would have received them in regular play. Thus, I would
consider it cheating. If cheating with restored saved games is
savescumming to you, then it is savescumming.

